# danielpauls — Daniel Pauls' entire conversation, every quest he appears in.
#
# A quests/dialogue/ file: DIALOGUE blocks and NO QUEST block. The importer and
# Tools -> Content -> Validate Quests both refuse either mistake. See
# docs/reference/QUEST_TEXT_FORMAT.md.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS DANIEL PAULS' CONVERSATION. One DIALOGUE block per npcId across the whole
# quests/ tree: each import regenerates Dialogue_danielpauls.asset wholesale, so a second file
# declaring DIALOGUE danielpauls would clobber this one. Every future Daniel Pauls quest adds its
# nodes HERE, gated on its own quest id.
#
# The quests whose beats live in this file:
#   spark_of_talent        - quests/spark_of_talent.quest        (granted and completed here)
#   daniel_pauls_quest_one - quests/daniel_pauls_quest_one.quest (completed here; granted by
#                            Councillor Mosley, quests/dialogue/councillormosley.quest)
#   check_out_the_church   - quests/check_out_the_church.quest   (granted at dpq1_speed; completed
#                            at cotc_scrapman, which also grants Quest 4)
#   investigate_weird_vape - quests/investigate_weird_vape.quest (Quest 4 pt 1: Daniel's stage-1 and
#                            stage-3 beats; completed at iwv_deliver, which grants part 2)
#   deliver_the_big_blue   - quests/deliver_the_big_blue.quest   (Quest 4 pt 2: Daniel's report;
#                            completed at dbb_chat, which also grants Quest 5)

DIALOGUE danielpauls

# Neutral root hub: Daniel greets neutrally on every interaction, and gated choices branch
# into quest-specific dialogues without re-playing the intro monologue.
NODE start
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Alright lad, what's occurring?
CHOICE Who are you then? -> intro_blaine
GATE: not-started spark_of_talent
CHOICE About that oddball... -> nudge
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 0
CHOICE I found him. Something weird happened. -> reward
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 1
CHOICE Councillor Mosley sent me back to you. -> dpq1_open
GATE: active daniel_pauls_quest_one
# check_out_the_church branch. Requires the makeshift vape (greys until carried), so it only opens
# once the player is back from the church with it. Daniel speaks first ("What is this contraption?").
CHOICE I found this weird vape at the church. -> cotc_show
GATE: active check_out_the_church
ITEM: makeshift_vape x1
# investigate_weird_vape, stage 1 — the player is back from Scrap Man with the "Big Blue" price.
# Daniel speaks first ("So what's he said?").
CHOICE I spoke to Scrap Man. -> iwv_bigblue
GATE: stage investigate_weird_vape 1
# investigate_weird_vape, stage 3 — the player is back with the gathered goods. Requires blueberries
# as a proxy (a choice can require only one item; the full three-item check is the Collect stage's
# job — its objective only flips to "head back" once all three are carried). Daniel speaks first
# ("Oh mate, amazing.").
CHOICE Here are the ingredients for the Big Blue. -> iwv_brew
GATE: stage investigate_weird_vape 3
ITEM: blueberries x2
# deliver_the_big_blue, stage 1 — the report after Scrap Man's reveal. Daniel speaks first
# ("Alright then, so what did you find out?").
CHOICE Scrap Man told me who's behind the vapes. -> dbb_report
GATE: stage deliver_the_big_blue 1
CHOICE Got any magic advice for me? -> done
GATE: complete spark_of_talent
CHOICE Catch you later.

NODE intro_blaine
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: David Blaine was my 3rd ever student. Second was a fella named Jesus. Now he didn't learn too much — I didn't know Spanish and he wasn't great with English, but he was a good trier.
CHOICE Uh, what? -> offer_open
CHOICE Not now, mate.

NODE offer_open
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: HEY YOU! I can sense it, you've got it. Do me a favour and I'll change your life!
CHOICE What are you on about? What are you up to? -> research
CHOICE Not now, weirdo.

NODE research
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: There's been a few suspect events. Sparks and bangs, strange folk acting aloof.
CHOICE Actually — saw a bloke get zapped by some smackhead outside the Joneses' last week. Thought I'd had some dodgy bud. -> sendoff
GRANT: spark_of_talent
CHOICE Right. I'll leave you to it.

NODE sendoff
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Haha! That wasn't the bud, son. That was magic. Please, do me a kindness. Find the oddball and have a word for me.

NODE nudge
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Come on! Get after him!

NODE reward
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Let's have it! I knew you had it in you, you've got the gift!
CHOICE So... what happens now? -> teach
# Gated to stage 1 so it cannot be re-picked once the quest completes (which would reopen the
# naming popup). The reward node is only reachable at stage 1 anyway; this makes the rule the
# validator checks explicit rather than relying on the entry gate.
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 1
TEACHSPARK
COMPLETE: spark_of_talent

NODE teach
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Right, now I invoke the 7 secret corners of the magic circle....... GUH........ feel that? Give it a name if you want, then shout it out and try it!

NODE done
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Careful where you sling spells, lad. Johnny Law comes a-knocking if you're too liberal with the lightning.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# daniel_pauls_quest_one - "Find the Magic Man".
#
# Reached from NODE start's  GATE: active daniel_pauls_quest_one  choice. The quest itself is
# granted by Councillor Mosley at his hand-in (quests/dialogue/councillormosley.quest, node
# nag_two), never here, and its definition is quests/daniel_pauls_quest_one.quest - one MANUAL
# stage, which nothing watches, so the COMPLETE: below is the only thing that can end it.
#
# One straight run of single-choice nodes: Daniel talks, the player prompts him on.

NODE dpq1_open
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Just the man. Right, well... I know you feel like you're on your own in all this magic lark.
CHOICE A bit, yeah. -> dpq1_help

NODE dpq1_help
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Well, there's a way you can help me out while getting some practice in.
CHOICE Go on. -> dpq1_church

NODE dpq1_church
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: The abandoned church next to the castle has had its copper stripped from the roof.
CHOICE And that's out of the ordinary around here? -> dpq1_speed

NODE dpq1_speed
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Well, no. But it's the speed of it. I was there just the day before. Then by the morning, poof — completely stripped clean.
# This one choice both completes "Find the Magic Man" and grants Quest 3, "Check Out the Church" -
# the same shape as councillormosley.quest's nag_two, which completes one quest and grants the next
# from a single choice. By the time Daniel says his closing line, the journal has swapped one quest
# for the next, so it clears as he briefs you rather than a beat later.
CHOICE Sounds like an organized crew. -> dpq1_close
COMPLETE: daniel_pauls_quest_one
GRANT: check_out_the_church

NODE dpq1_close
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: It's too big a church... something ain't right. Check it out for me, please. Few quid in it for you too.
# This choice must have no  ->  : that is what ends a conversation. Without one this node has no
# exit, and DialogueManager would append its own - an ending nobody wrote, mid-conversation.
CHOICE Alright, I'll take a look.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# check_out_the_church - "Check Out the Church" (Quest 3).
#
# Reached from NODE start's  GATE: active check_out_the_church  choice (which also requires the
# makeshift vape). The player has fought through the church and is showing Daniel what a Neek was
# carrying. The vape is NOT consumed - it travels on to Scrap Man in the Quest 4 arc.

NODE cotc_show
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: What in God's name is this contraption? Looks like a vape crossed with a car battery.
# The player says nothing scripted here - just a click onward.
CHOICE Found it on one of the Neeks in the church. -> cotc_scrapman

NODE cotc_scrapman
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Give Scrap Man a shout for me down south. He knows every piece of junk in London.
# This one choice completes Check Out the Church and grants the Quest 4 arc's first quest,
# investigate_weird_vape - the same shape as dpq1_speed above.
CHOICE On it.
COMPLETE: check_out_the_church
GRANT: investigate_weird_vape

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# investigate_weird_vape - "Investigate the Weird Vape" (Quest 4, part 1). Daniel's two beats:
#   stage 1 (iwv_bigblue) - he hears the "Big Blue" price and lists the ingredients.
#   stage 3 (iwv_brew)    - he combines the gathered goods, hands over the Big Blue, sends you back
#                           to Scrap Man. This completes part 1 and grants part 2.

NODE iwv_bigblue
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: So what did Scrap Man say?
CHOICE He wants a 'Big Blue' concoction before he spills anything. -> iwv_bits

NODE iwv_bits
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Fuck's sake. Right, I'm gonna need some bits to brew that up.
CHOICE You've got legs, haven't you? -> iwv_guild

NODE iwv_guild
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Come on, brew him a good batch and you're in the guild.
CHOICE Guild? What guild? -> iwv_list

NODE iwv_list
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: The Alchemists' Guild! Come on. Here's the list. You can grab all of it over in the old bus station.
CHOICE Sounds like a lovely day out. -> iwv_diary

NODE iwv_diary
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Directions are in your diary. I'll sort you some proper cash when you get back too.
# Ends the conversation. This is stage 1 (TalkTo danielpauls), which advances to stage 2 on the
# interact, so the objective becomes "clear the Neeks" as the chat closes.
CHOICE Fine, fine. Be right back.

NODE iwv_brew
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Oh mate, amazing! You absolute legend. Right, I'm gonna brew these into a potion for Scrap Man now. Give me a second.
CHOICE Go ahead. -> iwv_stir

NODE iwv_stir
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: *He begins to stir and crush the ingredients in his pestle and mortar vigorously until a strange luminous blue liquid emerges.*
# The script's "[Next]" beat here - the player just clicks on.
CHOICE *watch him work* -> iwv_distill

NODE iwv_distill
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: *He distills the glowing blue liquid into a janky-looking flask and hands it over.*
CHOICE [Take the suspicious Big Blue flask] -> iwv_deliver

NODE iwv_deliver
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Right, get that over to Scrap Man and bring back whatever gossip he's sitting on. Cheers, lad.
# Completes part 1 (the reward, the Big Blue, is paid on this) and grants part 2. Ends the chat.
CHOICE See you in a bit.
COMPLETE: investigate_weird_vape
GRANT: deliver_the_big_blue

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# deliver_the_big_blue - "Deliver the Big Blue" (Quest 4, part 2). Daniel's one beat:
#   stage 1 (dbb_report) - the report after Scrap Man's reveal. Completes part 2, pays the cash,
#                          and grants Quest 5 (wtf_mosley) - go and confront Mosley.

NODE dbb_report
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Alright then, what did Scrap Man say?
CHOICE Mosley's been buying dodgy vapes off the Spartans, who got them imported from China. It's what's driving the Neeks feral. -> dbb_chat

NODE dbb_chat
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: What? China? Mosley hates foreign gear! Nah, he can't be that desperate. Please, go have a word with him. Here's your cash for the info, but you've got to sort him out. That can't be right.
# Ends the chat (no ->), completes part 2 and grants Quest 5.
CHOICE I'll go confront him.
COMPLETE: deliver_the_big_blue
GRANT: wtf_mosley
